    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a daily-registration limit on `POST /api/owners` that rejects creating an owner once 100 or more owners have already been registered today (by `registrationDate`), responding **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\nFollowing the existing OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (modeled on the parallel `EnsureCityCapacity` rule), I added:\n\n1. **`EnsureDailyLimit`** (`.../function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws `DailyLimitReachedException` when the count is \u2265 100. Runs before `SaveOwner`, so it excludes the owner being created.\n\n2. **`DailyLimitReachedException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) \u2014 carries the current count.\n\n3. **`DailyLimitReachedExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds 429 with a `ProblemDetail` body, consistent with the other escalation handlers.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/...DailyLimitReachedException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the `ensureDailyLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureCityCapacity` and `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, then expect the 101st to return 429) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
